{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"box","type":"group","x":1680,"y":-960,"width":1300,"height":1600,"label":"THE BOX — one Docker container. This is the boundary."},
		{"id":"host","type":"group","x":-1500,"y":-700,"width":1100,"height":1450,"label":"HOST — the Sandbox User's own computer (trusted)"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"# Agentbox — how it works\n\nA colleague who doesn't code gets a coding agent to play with, in a box that can't hurt their laptop or reach company systems.\n\n**Read it left to right.** The Launcher is trusted host code. Everything past the red door runs inside the container — and the container *is* the permission boundary, which is why the agent runs with its own guardrails off.","x":-1500,"y":-1080,"width":1100,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"launcher","type":"text","text":"## Launcher  (Electron)\n\nThe whole interface. Hides Docker.\n\n- starts the Engine and the Box\n- the Project home screen\n- per-Project panel: Upload, Save, Preview\n- quit ⇒ `docker stop`","x":-1440,"y":-620,"width":980,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"window","type":"text","text":"## Session window\n\nLauncher-owned: no URL bar, no tabs, one per Project.\nJust a view of a terminal that lives in the Box.","x":-1440,"y":-300,"width":980,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"token","type":"text","text":"## GitHub token  🔑\n\nThe user's own account, OAuth device flow, encrypted in the OS keystore.\n\n**It never enters the Box.** Save to GitHub runs two throwaway containers: one has the files and no token, the other has the token and no files.","x":-1440,"y":-40,"width":980,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"engine","type":"text","text":"## Engine\n\nThe headless container runtime — Colima (macOS) / Podman-WSL2 (Windows).\nCapped at ~4 CPU / 6 GB / 25 GB.","x":-1440,"y":240,"width":980,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"files","type":"text","text":"## Their own files\n\n**Upload** — pick files, copied in.\n**Import** — a whole folder becomes a Project.\n**Export** — documents copied back out, marked untrusted so Gatekeeper/SmartScreen apply.\n\nCopies only. Nothing is ever mounted live.","x":-1440,"y":470,"width":980,"height":230},
		{"id":"tmux","type":"text","text":"## tmux — one session per Project\n\nThe source of truth. Close the window, the work keeps running.","x":1820,"y":-80,"width":420,"height":190,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"workspace","type":"text","text":"## Workspace  💾\n\n`/workspace/<slug>` on a named volume.\nThe only place work lives — survives restarts and rebuilds. No host mount.","x":2300,"y":-80,"width":420,"height":190,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"agent","type":"text","text":"## The agent\n\n**Claude Code** or **Codex** — one app-level setting.\n\nRuns with its own guardrails off: the walls around it are real, so a per-action prompt would only teach the user to click Yes.","x":1820,"y":170,"width":420,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"home","type":"text","text":"## `/home/sandbox`  💾\n\nThe agent login token — their own subscription seat, signed in from inside the Box.\n\nGrants that coding agent and nothing else.","x":2300,"y":170,"width":420,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"db","type":"text","text":"## Postgres\n\nA sibling container on an internal network with no route out.","x":2300,"y":460,"width":420,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"entry","type":"text","text":"## entrypoint.sh\n\nBoot order, and the order matters:\n\n1. **firewall first**\n2. login bridge (`:1455`)\n3. the web console\n4. stay alive","x":1820,"y":-920,"width":420,"height":250,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"egress","type":"text","text":"## Egress Policy  🧱\n\nThe public internet: **open** (the agent needs its vendor).\n\nYour LAN, the host, anything private: **blocked**.","x":2300,"y":-920,"width":420,"height":250,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"console","type":"text","text":"## Web console  `:7681`\n\nLoopback only — never the LAN.\nServes the terminal page and its WebSocket.","x":1820,"y":-620,"width":420,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"funnel","type":"text","text":"## `agentbox-session <slug>`  ⟵ THE funnel\n\nThe single way any Project ever starts, from either direction:\n\ncheck the slug shape → require `.agentbox/project.json` → `tmux new-session -A` → start the agent named in that file.\n\nDriven only by data on the volume, so a crafted slug can't spawn anything.","x":1820,"y":-370,"width":900,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"internet","type":"text","text":"## The public internet\n\n✅ reachable\n\nIt has to be — that's where the agent's vendor is.","x":3140,"y":-920,"width":320,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"lan","type":"text","text":"## Your LAN, your laptop, on-prem systems\n\n⛔ blocked at the firewall\n\nand no company credential is in there to use anyway.","x":3140,"y":-620,"width":320,"height":250,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"door","type":"text","text":"# 🚪\n## The one door\n\n`docker exec` / `docker cp`\n\nEverything that touches the Box goes through here — **one operation at a time** (the Box Gate), so an Update can't recreate the container out from under a half-finished Import.\n\nEvery command has a deadline.","x":520,"y":-255,"width":300,"height":420,"color":"1"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"e0","fromNode":"launcher","fromSide":"left","toNode":"engine","toSide":"left","label":"starts"},
